letters in the word ALGORITHMS, so $n=10.$ We want to select $5$ of those letters to make a $5$-letter word, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different made-up words is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{10}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{10!}{(10-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =30\\,240.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122476/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "256d3a08-0ade-51e9-887b-67250d5fae21"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122476"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84989/selection/ff778f6775302ce8b078ed4b299e814a54c571c5f88ede03fa1c06ca483a615f" :answer/id #uuid "ac201ec2-4bdd-5fe1-ac0f-ea069759e1c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,320" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84989/selection/f4994bdc324858da0f0956ee332239eb8763040a95dc2314c1ffcf1abbbccdbb" :answer/id #uuid "75fef02b-3c27-52fe-b77f-836d05e69a72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "729" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84989/selection/405774b6d78603d00b67b8e1d1e1f06704f5b811c6c62f2dffa37d5d917749d9" :answer/id #uuid "077d02ca-2f24-51b0-b738-20c8ed813099" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32\\,760" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84989/selection/ff4b0ca2de61be0550b98fed0c1f294dc6c493d2e89867a04289dde7dc989d86" :answer/id #uuid "698c54ef-2cd1-5852-aad3-b48d02ff62f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,730" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84989/selection/c1cbb22285b7914b6094319fb5b652431afac497c7cbdd14cf172d6d3c763a8a" :answer/id #uuid "ca512c0d-49dc-5659-b41c-73531cefda4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "504" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84989/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba856cea-ef34-5547-bea6-33cac1210bdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84989/selection/ff778f6775302ce8b078ed4b299e814a54c571c5f88ede03fa1c06ca483a615f" :answer-field/choices ["q-84989/selection/ff778f6775302ce8b078ed4b299e814a54c571c5f88ede03fa1c06ca483a615f" "q-84989/selection/f4994bdc324858da0f0956ee332239eb8763040a95dc2314c1ffcf1abbbccdbb" "q-84989/selection/405774b6d78603d00b67b8e1d1e1f06704f5b811c6c62f2dffa37d5d917749d9" "q-84989/selection/ff4b0ca2de61be0550b98fed0c1f294dc6c493d2e89867a04289dde7dc989d86" "q-84989/selection/c1cbb22285b7914b6094319fb5b652431afac497c7cbdd14cf172d6d3c763a8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84989" :question/id #uuid "e6dff14c-3932-5c6a-a562-7f8077a1018e" :question/math-academy-id "q-84989" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The $12$ members of a student council are asked to elect among themselves a leadership team: a president, a vice-president, and a secretary. How many different leadership teams are possible?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $12$ members to choose from, so $n=12.$ We want to select $3$ of those members to be in the leadership team, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different $3$-member leadership teams is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{12}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{12!}{(12-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12!}{9!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 11\\cdot 10\\cdot \\cancel{9!}}{\\cancel{9!}} \\\\  & =12\\cdot 11\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =1\\,320.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84989/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "256d3a08-0ade-51e9-887b-67250d5fae21"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84989"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
